etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176299\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: geo.tv\nSLUG: 667987-iran-to-travel-to-us-day-before-its-first-world-cup-match\nTEXT: Iran\'s football federation announced its national team\'s schedule for the group stage of the 2026 World Cup, with players obtaining visas to enter the US. However, not all delegation members received their visas, sparking a visa dispute just days before the tournament starts. The team will travel to the US on a charter flight, with matches in Los Angeles and Seattle. Iran\'s Sports Minister Ahmad Donyamali warned against displaying certain symbols during matches, stating that team officials will stop the game if they see any flags or symbols other than those of the Islamic Republic of Iran. The team will play New Zealand in Los Angeles on June 15, followed by Belgium in the same city on June 21 and Egypt in Seattle on June 26.\n\nID: 4176662\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: iran-to-be-based-in-mexico-and-fly-into-usa-on-day-before-fifa-world-cup-2026-opener-ws-lno-10139946-html\nTEXT: Iran\'s national football team will base itself in Tijuana, Mexico, for the 2026 FIFA World Cup and play group games in the United States amid a visa dispute. The team will fly to Los Angeles on June 14, the day before their opening group-stage match against New Zealand. Despite playing all three of their first-round matches in the US, 15 members of their support staff were denied visas. Iran\'s Sports Minister, Ahmad Donyamali, warned that matches may be stopped if banned symbols or slogans appear in the stadiums. The team will travel to host cities one day before matches, and for the following two matches, they will be at the host venue two days before the game.\n\n\n',)
