ntury archaeological site at Al Luluyah Beach. The Dh8 million heritage project, scheduled for completion within six months, will feature 20 traditionally styled shops alongside restaurants, cafes, visitor seating and shaded walkways throughout the archaeological zone.\n\n\n',)
