etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4176782\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: nitish-kumar-praises-pm-narendra-modi-longest-serving-elected-prime-minister-tenure-indian-democracy-nda-ws-l-10140039-html\nTEXT: Former Bihar Chief Minister Nitish Kumar praises PM Narendra Modi for his longest-serving tenure as elected Prime Minister, citing his emphasis on implementation and delivery. Kumar credits Modi\'s governance model for reducing the gap between policymaking and implementation, particularly through technology, direct benefit transfers, and monitoring mechanisms. He also commends Modi\'s approach to federalism, citing support extended to Bihar through recent Union Budgets. Kumar notes that Modi has showcased Bihar\'s heritage internationally and ensured Bharat Ratna for former Bihar chief minister Karpoori Thakur. The article coincides with Modi completing 4,399 consecutive days in office, surpassing Nehru\'s record.\n\nID: 4176713\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: lokmattimes.com\nSLUG: pm-modi-became-prime-minister-through-peoples-mandate-not-privilege-union-minister-giriraj-singh\nTEXT: Union Minister Giriraj Singh stated that Prime Minister Narendra Modi became India\'s longest-serving democratically elected Prime Minister through the people\'s mandate, not privilege. This was highlighted during celebrations marking 12 years of Modi\'s government at the Centre, where he offered prayers at a Hanuman temple. Singh praised Modi\'s journey and contributions to the country, noting his rise to the highest elected office was due to popular support rather than privilege.\n\nID: 4176783\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: pm-modi-12-years-prime-minister-public-service-good-governance-longest-serving-prime-minister-nda-meeting-ws-l-10140146-html\nTEXT: Prime Minister Narendra Modi marked a record-breaking 12 years in office, becoming India\'s longest-serving Prime Minister. In a post on X, Modi emphasized the importance of public service as the ultimate measure of good governance. He stressed that humility, dedication, and a strong sense of duty are essential to earning the trust of the people. This marks 4,399 days in office, surpassing former Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru\'s record of 4,398 consecutive days.\n\nID: 4176781\nCREATED: 2026-06-10\nDOMAIN: news18.com\nSLUG: man-of-destiny-for-india-venkaiah-naidu-hails-pm-modi-as-he-becomes-longest-serving-elected-pm-ws-l-10139968-html\nTEXT: Former Vice President M Venkaiah Naidu hailed Prime Minister Narendra Modi as the "Man of Destiny for India" after he became the longest-serving elected PM, surpassing Jawaharlal Nehru\'s record. Naidu praised Modi\'s leadership and governance record, saying India has reached a new level under his tenure. Born to parents of modest means, Modi worked as a tea vendor in Vadnagar, Gujarat, before rising to occupy the country\'s highest elected office.\n\n\n',)
